      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can be verbose and tedious to do this mapping at the level of `fdt.compatible_nodes` and `node.getprop_cells`.\n\nActually my idea is to intervene at a higher level, not to touch the functions that return `libfdt::Result` such as\n```\nfn read_pci_info_from(fdt: \u0026Fdt) -\u003e libfdt::Result\u003cPciInfo\u003e\nfn patch_pci_info(fdt: \u0026mut Fdt, pci_info: \u0026PciInfo) -\u003e libfdt::Result\u003c()\u003e\n```\nI\u0027ll just add a tag to error to mark that these are the `FdtError` from the `PCI` node for example. So the caller will switch from \n```\npatch_pci_info(fdt, \u0026info.pci_info).map_err(|e| {\n        error!(\"Failed to patch pci info to DT: {e}\");\n        RebootReason::InvalidFdt\n    })?;\n```\nto\n```\npatch_pci_info(fdt, \u0026info.pci_info).map_err(|e| FdtValidationError::ParsingNodeFailed(\"PCI\", FdtError) \n```",
